From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rudi Heitbaum <rudi@heitbaum.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 00:58:09 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: imx8mq-phanbell: describe the QCA6174 Bluetooth

The Coral Dev Board's QCA6174 has its Bluetooth side on uart2 with flow
control, and a power line on gpio3 line 6. Describe it with the serdev
binding so hci_qca can drive it.

The vendor devicetree does not use serdev - it has a downstream
"fsl,mxc_bt_rfkill" shim and leaves the rest to userspace hciattach -
but it does give the wiring. Its bt-power-gpios names gpio3 line 6, and
its uart2 pinctrl group mixes the four uart pins in with that same GPIO
as NAND_DATA00_GPIO3_IO6. Note the flow control pins are muxed from the
UART4 pads, not the UART2 ones.

uart2 has to be reparented off the 25MHz oscillator. hci_qca declares
oper_speed 3000000 and hci_uart_setup() applies it immediately after the
115200 init speed, but the imx uart caps out at uartclk/16, so on the
default parent the host lands at 1.5625MHz while the controller has
moved to 3MHz. The result is a stream of "Frame reassembly failed
(-84)" and "command 0xfc00 tx timeout". SYS1_PLL_80M gives 5MHz of
headroom and follows imx8mq-hummingboard-pulse and
imx8mq-kontron-pitx-imx8m, which reparent their uarts the same way.

Signed-off-by: Rudi Heitbaum <rudi@heitbaum.com>
---
 .../boot/dts/freescale/imx8mq-phanbell.dts    | 32 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 32 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx8mq-phanbell.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx8mq-phanbell.dts
index 5fed8f223e64..12cc7c83f50e 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx8mq-phanbell.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx8mq-phanbell.dts
@@ -481,6 +481,23 @@ &uart1 {
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+&uart2 {
+	pinctrl-names = "default";
+	pinctrl-0 = <&pinctrl_uart2>;
+	assigned-clocks = <&clk IMX8MQ_CLK_UART2>;
+	assigned-clock-parents = <&clk IMX8MQ_SYS1_PLL_80M>;
+	uart-has-rtscts;
+	status = "okay";
+
+	bluetooth {
+		compatible = "qcom,qca6174-bt";
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+		pinctrl-0 = <&pinctrl_bt>;
+		enable-gpios = <&gpio3 6 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		clocks = <&pmic>;
+	};
+};
+
 &usdhc1 {
 	pinctrl-names = "default", "state_100mhz", "state_200mhz";
 	pinctrl-0 = <&pinctrl_usdhc1>;
@@ -629,6 +646,21 @@ MX8MQ_IOMUXC_GPIO1_IO03_GPIO1_IO3	0x41
 		>;
 	};
 
+	pinctrl_bt: btgrp {
+		fsl,pins = <
+			MX8MQ_IOMUXC_NAND_DATA00_GPIO3_IO6	0x19
+		>;
+	};
+
+	pinctrl_uart2: uart2grp {
+		fsl,pins = <
+			MX8MQ_IOMUXC_UART2_RXD_UART2_DCE_RX	0x49
+			MX8MQ_IOMUXC_UART2_TXD_UART2_DCE_TX	0x49
+			MX8MQ_IOMUXC_UART4_RXD_UART2_DCE_CTS_B	0x49
+			MX8MQ_IOMUXC_UART4_TXD_UART2_DCE_RTS_B	0x49
+		>;
+	};
+
 	pinctrl_uart1: uart1grp {
 		fsl,pins = <
 			MX8MQ_IOMUXC_UART1_RXD_UART1_DCE_RX		0x49
-- 
2.47.1

